Z||000001||qwikgta||08-27-2001||07:23 PM||||Welcome,<BR>  Use the search function and look for engines or engine swaps ect...  The reason no one answered is that we have to tell every new person about the search function.  If you dont find what you want, then reask a question but please be more specific.<P>Good luck<P>Rob||||reg||1
Z||000002||skitime||08-27-2001||07:58 PM||||Hey, welcome to the forum.  You come to the right place for answers and most are better than the first.  Most late model front wheel drive GM engines can be put in your Fiero and bolt to the trans. You have to transfer and adapt the donors car computer and some of the wiring with it. You have to decide how much power and how much money you want to spend.  Have fun deciding which engine since I really can't decide which one I want either.<P><P>------------------<BR><UL TYPE=SQUARE><BR><LI>Red 88 GT T-TOP<BR><LI>Red 86 GT<BR></UL> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/signature-1.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000003||qwikgta||08-27-2001||10:11 PM||||Ski..  <BR>  My point is that if used the search function will answer most questions.  Most new people don't even know it is there. I was informed about the search function and was glad someone pointed it out to me, it answered many questions, I was not trying to be rude, just quick and to the point.  Engine swaps are one of the most discussed threads here, you could spend a while going over every one, one by one.  Let him/her read the other threads and then come back with the "20" questions that will follow.<P>Rob<p>[This message has been edited by qwikgta (edited 08-27-2001).]||||reg||1
